<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 31 October, from 475 to 2011.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">475 <span class="tih-ago">1,551 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romulus Augustulus is proclaimed western Roman emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general Orestes installed his young son Romulus as emperor in the West. Less than a year later Odoacer deposed him, an event conventionally taken as the end of the Western Roman Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mainz" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mainz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1517 <span class="tih-ago">509 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther issues his Ninety-five Theses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Martin Luther sent his Ninety-five Theses against the sale of indulgences to the Archbishop of Mainz and, by tradition, posted them on the church door at Wittenberg. The debate they sparked became the Reformation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1864 <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nevada becomes the 36th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nevada was admitted to the Union during the Civil War, with Republicans keen on its votes for Lincoln's re-election and support for the 13th Amendment. It is still called the 'Battle Born State'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1956 <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France begin bombing Egypt over Suez</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French aircraft attacked Egyptian airfields after Egypt rejected their ultimatum to withdraw from the Suez Canal zone. US and Soviet pressure forced a humiliating withdrawal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1984 <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi is assassinated by her bodyguards</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Sikh bodyguards shot Prime Minister Indira Gandhi in her Delhi garden, months after she ordered the army into the Golden Temple at Amritsar. Anti-Sikh violence that followed killed about 3,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-nations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2011 <span class="tih-ago">15 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">World population reaches seven billion, UN estimates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The United Nations designated 31 October 2011 as the symbolic day the world's population reached seven billion. The total had doubled since the late 1960s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li></ol>
